! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260 TEST 8C -- "CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4
! CONDS" -- cases 1 and 2, PDF pp.76-78, octal 022546.00-022636.40.
! One unbroken half-word run of 114 rows.  (This deck's listing pages
! carry no printed page numbers; cite by PDF page.)
!
! THE CONTROLS.  programs/ax5b_160_test8c.strap already holds cases 3
! and 4, the mask-dependent pair that runs with the interruption system
! ENABLED.  These two run it DISABLED, and they are what makes the
! other two mean anything: they say what happens when nothing is
! supposed to happen.
!
! THE TEST'S OWN TITLE, PDF p.76 at 022546.00, verbatim:
!
!   I60127 LVI,$X1,I60AD1  -TEST 8C CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4 CONDS,
!                          -1. DISABL MASK 0 FETCH OK IND NO INT
!                          -2. DIAABL MASK 1 FETCH OK NO IND NO INT
!                          -3. ENABLE MASK 0 FETCH OK IND ON NO INT
!                          -4. ENABLE MASK 1 NO FETCH IND ON INTRPT
!
! LINE 1'S "IND" IS WRONG, AND THIS TRANSCRIPTION SETTLES IT.  The
! question was open in this project: line 1 reads "FETCH OK IND NO INT"
! while line 2 reads "FETCH OK NO IND NO INT", and the two cases are
! otherwise the same experiment at two mask values.  The code says NO
! IND for both.  The decisive evidence is not case 1 read alone -- it
! is case 1 read against case 2:
!
!   * The two cases' indicator branches are BIT-IDENTICAL in polarity.
!     Case 1: BZDFZ -> 22560.12 44, BZIFZ -> 22574.12 C4.
!     Case 2: BZDFZ -> 22615.52 44, BZIFZ -> 22632.12 C4.
!     Same 44 / C4 low byte, same branch-on-zero bit.  Whatever BZ's
!     polarity is, cases 1 and 2 assert the SAME thing about the
!     indicator -- so "IND" on line 1 cannot be right unless "NO IND"
!     on line 2 is also wrong.
!
!   * The failure text inverts exactly where the expectation inverts.
!     Cases 1 and 2 both print "-CAUSES DF TO BE SET, NO INT."  Case 3
!     -- the case whose header line says "IND ON" -- prints "-CAUSES DF
!     NOT TO BE SET, NO INT."  A SIC,SEN / B,SERS pair is an error
!     report, so the text names the anomaly: cases 1 and 2 report DF
!     having been set, case 3 reports it not having been.
!
!   * The header block is demonstrably typo-prone: line 2 spells
!     DISABL as "DIAABL".  Line 1 is missing its "NO".
!
! Independently, the same reading falls out of the mnemonics: the
! grammar is B[Z]<indicator>[Z], the leading Z branches when the
! indicator is OFF, and the branch is the OK path in both cases while
! the fall-through is the error.  See the indicator-number decode
! below, which is a free check on the read.
!
! CASES 1 AND 2 ARE NOT REDUNDANT.  With the system disabled the deck
! asserts the mask bit is IRRELEVANT.  Case 2 runs with DF's and IF's
! mask bits set to ONE and still demands the fetch PROCEED --
! "-UNABLE TO FETCH ABOVE UB WITH / -MASK 1, SYSTEM DISABLED." and
! "-INSTRUCT FETCHED BELOW LB, DISABLED, / -MASK 1, WAS NOPED." -- where
! case 4 (enabled, mask 1) demands the same fetch be SUPPRESSED.  The
! pair is the deck's statement that disabled means: no suppression, no
! indicator, no interrupt, whatever the mask says.
!
! HOW THE SYSTEM IS DISABLED.  BE and BD are the enable/disable
! branches.  Cases 3 and 4 reach their offending fetch through
! "BE,$+.32"; these two reach it through "BD,$+.32" at 022550.00 and
! 022605.00, and every recovery branch in the block is a BD as well.
!
! THE OFFENDING FETCHES are arranged as in cases 3 and 4.  For DF,
! "LV,$X3,I60AD3" reads a word above UB (UB was just set from X1 =
! I60AD1).  For IF, "SV,$X2,$LB" sets the LOWER boundary to the label
! that follows, so the half-words just before it are fetched from a
! protected area as control falls through.  The did-it-execute probe is
! "LX,$X2,0": it loads X2 from word zero, and LX,$X2,$X2 plus a
! value-zero branch afterwards says whether it ran.
!
! CNOP IS ALIGNMENT-DEPENDENT, AND HERE IT IS INVERTED RELATIVE TO THE
! SIBLING FILE.  Keep it as CNOP; do not hand-expand it.
!   case 1: SV,$X2,$UB sits at 022567.00, so the next half-word
!           022567.40 is NOT word-aligned and CNOP EMITS a filler NOP
!           (0.30 00) there.  57 source lines, 57 machine-code rows.
!   case 2: SV,$X2,$UB sits at 022625.40, so 022626.00 is already
!           word-aligned and CNOP EMITS NOTHING -- the address column
!           steps straight from 022625.40 to 022626.00.  58 source
!           lines, 57 machine-code rows.
! In cases 3 and 4 the silent one was the EARLIER case; here it is the
! LATER one.  That inversion is the cleanest demonstration available
! that CNOP is a function of alignment and not a fixed emission.
!
! THE INDICATOR NUMBERS ARE IN THE PRINT, straddling the two fields.
! The indicator number sits at bits 19-24; bits 18-23 print as the
! octal pair and bit 24 is the top bit of the hex pair.
!   BZDFZ  "12 44": 001010 / 0x44=01000100 -> bits19-24 = 010100 = 20
!   BZIFZ  "12 C4": 001010 / 0xC4=11000100 -> bits19-24 = 010101 = 21
! DF is 20 and IF is 21, said by the deck, matching the sibling file
! and the mask bits (BIT20, BIT21) case 2 loads.
!
! A FIFTH BIT-TABLE CONFIRMATION.  024522 + n gives BIT12 -> 024536,
! printed at 022601.40 as "24536.32 B0".  The sibling file confirmed
! BIT14/BIT20/BIT21/BIT57 the same way; case 1's continuity word is
! bit 12, case 3's is bit 14.
!
! ENCODING ONLY.  Running it needs SSIP's I60S1/I60SX1 harness, the
! 64-word interrupt table at I60IT, and IF -- which this model does not
! implement at all.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_160_test8c_disabled_listing.py.

        SLC, (8)22546.00
!
! ---- CASE 1: disabled, mask 0 -- neither indicator may set (PDF p.76)
I60127 LVI, $X1, I60AD1           ! -TEST 8C CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4 CONDS,
        LX,  $X2, LBIT57            ! -1. DISABL MASK 0 FETCH OK IND NO INT
        SX,  $X2, 3.0               ! -2. DIAABL MASK 1 FETCH OK NO IND NO INT
        Z,   I60AD3                ! -3. ENABLE MASK 0 FETCH OK IND ON NO INT
        BD,  $+.32                  ! -4. ENABLE MASK 1 NO FETCH IND ON INTRPT
        Z,   $MASK                  ! mask 0 for this case
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1
        Z,   $IND
        LVI, $X3, (8)777777.40
        LVI, $X4, LINT
        LRI, $X4, I60IT
        LVI, $X5, I60128
        SVA, $X5, I60107
        SV,  $X1, $UB
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LV,  $X3, I60AD3           ! the fetch ABOVE UB
        BZDFZ, $+1.32               ! DF must be OFF
        SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCH ABOVE UB, DISABLED, MASK 0,
        B,   SERS                   ! -CAUSES DF TO BE SET, NO INT.
        BD,  $+1.32
I60128 SIC, SEN                    ! -ENTER HERE FROM INT.
        B,   SERS                   ! -INT ON DF, DISABLED MASK 0, FETCH
                                    ! -ABOVE UB.   (comment-only line)
        SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X3, $X3
        BXVZ, $+1.32                ! the fetch must have LANDED
        SIC, SEN                    ! -UNABLE TO FETCH ABOVE UB WITH
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 0, SYSTEM DISABLED.
        LVI, $X2, I60129
        SV,  $X2, $LB               ! lower boundary := I60129
        LVI, $X2, I60130
        SVA, $X2, I60107
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LVI, $X2, (8)777777.0
        SV,  $X2, $UB
        CNOP                        ! emits a NOP here: 022567.40 is odd
        LX,  $X2, 0                 ! fetched BELOW LB
        NOP
I60129 BZIFZ, I60131              ! IF must be OFF
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB SETS
        B,   SERS                   ! -IF, NO INT, MASK 0, DISABLED.
        BD,  I60131
I60130 SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB CAUSES
        B,   SERS                   ! -INT, MASK 0, DISABLED.
I60131 SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X2, $X2
        BXVZ, $+1.32                ! disabled: the fetch PROCEEDS
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCHED BELOW LB, DISABLED,
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 0, WAS NOPED.
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I60127
        SIC, LSEN0+.32
        B,   LSSW
        BD,  $+.32                  ! the page prints "BD,$+.32." -- the
                                    !   trailing period is not encoded:
                                    !   22601.04 00 is plain $+.32
!
! ---- the continuity bridge on PDF p.77 (case 1 done = bit 12) ----
        LX,  $X13, IC260           ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+,  $X13, LBIT12
        SX,  $X13, IC260
!
! ---- CASE 2: disabled, mask 1 -- same verdict, mask made no
!      difference (PDF p.78)
I60132 BD,  $+.32                  ! -TEST 8C, CASE 2.
        LVI, $X1, I60AD1
        LX,  $X2, LBIT57
        SX,  $X2, 3.0
        Z,   I60AD3
        BD,  $+.32
        LX,  $X2, LBIT20            ! DF's mask bit
        SX,  $X2, $MASK             !   ... set to ONE
        SIC, I60SX1
        B,   I60S1
        Z,   $IND
        LVI, $X3, (8)777777.40
        LVI, $X4, LINT
        LRI, $X4, I60IT
        LVI, $X5, I60133
        SVA, $X5, I60107
        SV,  $X1, $UB
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LV,  $X3, I60AD3           ! the fetch ABOVE UB
        BZDFZ, $+1.32               ! DF must be OFF, mask 1 or not
        SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCH ABOVE UB, DISABLED, MASK 1,
        B,   SERS                   ! -CAUSES DF TO BE SET, NO INT.
        BD,  $+1.32
I60133 SIC, SEN                    ! -FETCH ABOVE UB, DISABLED, MASK 1, CAUSES
        B,   SERS                   ! -INTERRUPT.
        SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X3, $X3
        BXVZ, $+1.32                ! disabled: the fetch LANDS even at mask 1
        SIC, SEN                    ! -UNABLE TO FETCH ABOVE UB WITH
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 1, SYSTEM DISABLED.
        LVI, $X2, I60134
        SV,  $X2, $LB               ! lower boundary := I60134
        LX,  $X2, LBIT21            ! IF's mask bit
        SX,  $X2, $MASK             !   ... set to ONE
        LVI, $X2, I60135
        SVA, $X2, I60107
        SR,  $X4, $IA
        LVI, $X2, (8)777777.0
        SV,  $X2, $UB
        CNOP                        ! emits NOTHING here: 022626.00 is even
        LX,  $X2, 0                 ! fetched BELOW LB
        NOP
I60134 BZIFZ, I60136              ! IF must be OFF
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB SETS
        B,   SERS                   ! -IF, NO INT, MASK 1, DISABLED.
        BD,  I60136
I60135 SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCH BELOW LB CAUSES
        B,   SERS                   ! -INT, MASK 1, DISABLED.
I60136 SV,  $X4, $IA
        LX,  $X2, $X2
        BXVZ, $+1.32                ! disabled: the fetch PROCEEDS
        SIC, SEN                    ! -INSTRUCT FETCHED BELOW LB, DISABLED,
        B,   SERS                   ! -MASK 1, WAS NOPED.
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I60132
        SIC, LSEN0+.32
        B,   LSSW                   ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
!
! ---- externals, SYN'd at the addresses this listing's own encodings
!      give.  A SYN IS AN INPUT TO THE CHECK, NOT A WITNESS: the rows
!      naming these symbols were used to derive the SYN value, so those
!      rows re-test only the opcode and modifier bits.  The rows that
!      really check address placement are the ones naming I60127 ..
!      I60136, which are defined INSIDE the transcribed range.  Same
!      caveat verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py makes about I6088.
!      Each SYN was read off bit 18 of the octal pair of the row that
!      names it, so each is itself a checkable claim.
I60AD1 SYN, (8)23063.0             ! from LVI,$X1,I60AD1 = 23063.03 01
I60AD3 SYN, (8)23064.0             ! from Z,I60AD3       = 23064.22 00
I60107 SYN, (8)22372.0             ! from SVA,$X5,I60107 = 22372.13 D0
I60S1  SYN, (8)22741.0             ! SSIP save/restore
I60SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0
I60IT  SYN, (8)23201.0             ! the 64-word interrupt table
LINT    SYN, (8)1353.0
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0
LSEN0   SYN, (8)1311.0              ! the deck spells it SEN0
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0
LSSW    SYN, (8)1301.0              ! the deck spells it SSW
IC260  SYN, (8)22737.0             ! the continuity word
LBIT12  SYN, (8)24536.0             ! 024522 + 12 = case 1's continuity bit
LBIT20  SYN, (8)24546.0             ! 024522 + 20 = DF's bit
LBIT21  SYN, (8)24547.0             ! 024522 + 21 = IF's bit
LBIT57  SYN, (8)24613.0             ! 024522 + 57 = the boundary control bit
        END, I60127
